  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lily and Leo are in the garden. They play a zoo game. There is a lot of fun. \"Let's make a zoo song!\" says Lily. \"Yes! We can clap and jump,\" says Leo. Pip sits and looks at them. They sing and do it. The song is long.",
      "\"Tiger, tiger, open your mouth!\" \"Zebra, zebra, point to your nose!\" \"Monkey, monkey, clap your hands!\" \"Elephant, elephant, jump, jump, jump!\" \"Giraffe, giraffe, point to your head!\" \"Hippo, hippo, open your mouth!\" \"At the zoo, at the zoo!\" \"We can see the animals at the zoo!\"",
      "They sing the song again. It is a good song. Pip jumps and says, \"Woof!\" \"Is Pip a tiger?\" asks Leo. \"No, Pip is a dog!\" says Lily. They clap and clap. Mom looks from the window. She claps too. Can Pip sing? Leo is the monkey now. Lily is the zebra. Pip is the happy dog. It is a fun song!"
    ],
